ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: CHEBI:132089
  ontology_label: sodium glycerol 2-phosphate
  ontology_source: CHEBI
  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CultureBotHT
    notes: Imported from CultureBotHT. CAS-RN 154804-51-0 present, but no CHEBI entry
      exists (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite + PubChem CID synonyms). Curator can promote
      to a CHEBI primary if/when CHEBI adds the term.
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: anchor_cas_hydrate_records
    notes: Beta-Glycerophosphate disodium salt hydrate is a hydrate/salt with its
      own CAS and no exact ChEBI term; anchored to the parent CHEBI:17270 'glycerol
      2-phosphate' by narrowMatch per MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3 step 2. disodium
      salt hydrate of glycerol 2-phosphate
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:17270 (''glycerol 2-phosphate'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:
      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,
      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance
      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims
      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier
      are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'CAS154804-51-0 denotes beta/2-glycerophosphate disodium hydrate in the
      inspected supplier comparator and historical source label. Preserve this hydrate
      owner separately from CHEBI132089 sodium beta-glycerophosphate and the distinct
      fixed-water sibling. CHEBI132089 sodium glycerol2-phosphate is a closer verified
      parent than free-acid CHEBI17270: its definition is the disodium salt. Use NARROW_MATCH/broadMatch
      to132089, not exact identity and not tetrahydrate132092. Current CID44828775/SMILES/InChI
      place negative charge on terminal alcohols while leaving phosphate OH, and all
      current structure/formula fields impose one water. Supplier comparator instead
      gives phosphate disodium salt xH2O. Withdraw formula, SMILES, InChI and CID
      without guessing a replacement. Primary source references: https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/g9422;
      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/substance/sourceid/Sigma-Aldrich/G9422_SIGMA/JSON;
      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/154804-51-0/property/Title,MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON;
      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/17270/; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/132089/;
      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/132092/. Captures, exact
      input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed
      owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'
